# card pure-class-methods-2: a class's methods in Python's brace-less form, `def area(): side * side`
# (run-time instances: `warp test tests/types` runs them through warp pure, `warp test --self tests/types` through
# warp self)

# a_colon_method
is! 'class Square { side: int; def area(): side * side }; Square(3).area()' 9
is! 'class P { x: int; def next(): x + 1 }; P{x: 4}.next()' 5

# fields_a_space_lists
is! 'class person{name age:int; older(y) := age + y}; person("Ann", 40).older(2)' 42
is! 'class person{name age:int}; p = person("Ann", 40); p.name + " " + str(p.age)' 'Ann 40'
